Logical: KGHealthIntervention
Title: "Knowledge graph L1: Health intervention"
Description: "What a recommendation is about, and the hinge to L2. Corresponds to the DAK component smart-base defines as HealthInterventions — today `id`, `description[x]` and `reference 1..* DublinCore`, i.e. a bibliographic citation with no recommendation behind it. This class is what that citation should resolve to. Corresponds to HealthInterventions: identifier = HealthInterventions.id and description = HealthInterventions.description[x]; not a Parent because HealthInterventions requires reference 1..* DublinCore, which in the graph is an edge to a publication rather than a field. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/health-intervention."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* identifier 0..1 string "Health Intervention ID" "An identifier for the health intervention"
* name 0..1 string "Name" "Name of the health intervention, as listed."
* description 0..1 markdown "Description" "Description of the health intervention"

Logical: KGSchedule
Title: "Knowledge graph L1: Schedule"
Description: "A normative delivery schedule. Grounded: the BCG table cites \"WHO recommendations for routine immunization – summary tables\", which IS a schedule publication — the single most-cited L1 source in the immunization DAK. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/schedule."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* identifier 0..1 string "Identifier" "Identifier of the schedule, where the source gives one."
* name 0..1 string "Name" "Name of the schedule (a summary table's title)."
* scope 0..1 string "Scope" "Who or what the schedule covers, as stated."

Logical: KGScheduleEntry
Title: "Knowledge graph L1: Schedule entry"
Description: "One row of a schedule: which intervention, for whom, when, how many doses. This is the granularity a decision table actually consumes — the BCG rules turn on dose count, age and interval since a live vaccine. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/schedule-entry."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* antigen 0..1 string "Antigen" "The antigen or vaccine the row is about."
* doseNumber 0..1 string "Dose number" "Dose in the series as printed (\"1\", \"Booster 1\"). Text, because schedules label boosters rather than count them."
* series 0..1 string "Series" "Primary series or booster series, as stated."
* targetAge 0..1 string "Target age" "Age at which the dose is due, as stated."
* minimumInterval 0..1 string "Minimum interval" "Minimum interval since the previous dose, as stated."
* note 0..1 string "Note" "The row's footnote or remark, verbatim."

Logical: KGIndicator
Title: "Knowledge graph L1: Indicator"
Description: "A programme indicator defined normatively at L1. Distinct from the DAK's ProgramIndicator component, which is its L2 expression; that model already carries `references 0..* id` pointing at health intervention ids. Corresponds to ProgramIndicator: same element names and types (markdown), identifier = ProgramIndicator.id; not a Parent because ProgramIndicator makes name, definition, numerator, denominator and disaggregation 1..1 and an L1 indicator is recorded with what its source states. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/indicator."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* identifier 0..1 string "Indicator ID" "Identifier for the program indicator"
* name 0..1 string "Name" "Name of the indicator"
* definition 0..1 markdown "Definition" "Definition of what the indicator measures"
* numerator 0..1 markdown "Numerator" "Description of the numerator calculation"
* denominator 0..1 markdown "Denominator" "Description of the denominator calculation"
* disaggregation 0..1 markdown "Disaggregation" "Description of how the indicator should be disaggregated"

Logical: KGTerminologyCode
Parent: Coding
Title: "Knowledge graph L1: Terminology code"
Description: "A code in an external terminology — ICD-10, ICD-11, SNOMED CT, ATC, or a WHO classification such as CDHI. CROSS-REFERENCE ONLY. It records system, code and display, and asserts NOTHING about the terminology: no hierarchy, no subsumption, no synonyms, no post-coordination. The terminology has its own authority, its own release cycle and its own tooling, and a partial copy here would be wrong within one release. Resolve meaning against the terminology server, not against this graph. Derives from Coding (FHIR R4 core datatype); system, code, display, version are its elements. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/terminology-code."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"

Logical: KGCitation
Title: "Knowledge graph L1: Citation"
Description: "A citation string exactly as it appears in an L2 or L3 artefact, together with what it was resolved to. Grounded directly in the BCG table, where every rule's annotationEntry[1] reads \"WHO recommendations for routine immunization – summary tables (March 2023) (1)\" — a citation that no tool can currently follow. This class is where that string becomes a link, and where the fact that resolving it was a judgement gets recorded. text is verbatim. location is the artefact path plus the element id — e.g. the DMN rule id. numbering preserves the \"(1)\" back-reference into the source document's own bibliography. resolutionStatus is unresolved | resolved | ambiguous; ambiguous is a legitimate terminal state and must not be collapsed to resolved. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/citation."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* text 0..1 string "Text" "The citation string, VERBATIM as it appears in the citing artefact."
* location 0..1 string "Location" "The citing artefact's path plus the element id (a DMN rule id, a page)."
* numbering 0..1 string "Numbering" "The '(1)' back-reference into the citing document's own bibliography."
* resolutionStatus 0..1 code "Resolution status" "unresolved | resolved | ambiguous. Ambiguous is a legitimate terminal state."
* resolutionStatus from KGResolutionStatusVS (required)

Logical: KGExternalArtifact
Title: "Knowledge graph L1: External artefact"
Description: "An L2 or L3 artefact addressed by canonical URL — a BPMN process, a DMN decision table, a FHIR PlanDefinition. Deliberately opaque: it carries an IRI and a free-text kind, and this graph asserts nothing about its internal structure. That opacity is the boundary. The L2 and L3 subgraphs model those artefacts properly; L1 only needs to point. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/external-artifact."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* iri 0..1 uri "IRI" "Canonical URL or IRI of the L2 or L3 artefact."
* targetKind 0..1 string "Target kind" "What kind of artefact it is, free text (\"DMN decision table\", \"DAK component\")."
* version 0..1 string "Version" "Version of the artefact, where known."

Logical: KGEvidenceLocation
Title: "Knowledge graph: evidence location"
Description: "Where a node or edge came from in its source. Required on anything not mechanically derived."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* location 1..1 string "Location" "file:line, a spreadsheet sheet and cell, or a BPMN element id."
* quote 0..1 string "Quote" "Verbatim text from the source."
* artifact 0..1 string "Artifact" "The generated artifact affected, where one exists."

